  "2026-07-30T07:18:57.436Z","harness:codex","Tranche boundary: this PR exposes canonical visibility on command-scoped/full contracts and preserves the existing shared tier registry, MCP, completion, and generated-doc gates. CLI help routing and the one-field four-surface snapshot/budget proof remain; returning open without claiming the complete single-source migration."
  "2026-07-30T07:26:28.388Z","harness:codex","Token-efficiency evidence: command visibility and canonical identity remain available in command-scoped contracts, while unscoped/full projections omit repeated semantic rows. This preserves the visibility primitive without increasing the all-in-one context surface beyond its enforced budget."
  "2026-07-30T07:40:05.149Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/822 carries the cohesive SDK/CLI self-describing context-contract bundle. Initial implementation commit e1fabaa97; final exact-head checks and review evidence will be recorded in the PR because post-review tracker mutations would create a new unreviewed Git tree."
  "2026-07-30T08:15:44.636Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence for PR #822: the built-in list/triage intent now preserves governance and execution fields (priority, ownership, risk/confidence, scheduling, blocker and dependency context) while explicit caller projections still win. Packed CLI acceptance exercised the triage projection against a newly created item."
  "2026-08-16T10:44:19.101Z","harness:claude-code","Grammar ruling AC (recorded on pm-pbyu 2026-08-16) places the capability-family declaration here, beside the tier, because both are the same kind of contract data and both are consumed by the same four surfaces. Measured basis: PM_COMMAND_VISIBILITY_CONTRACTS declares a tier per command and nothing declares a family, so rewriting the four agent skill bundles for progressive disclosure required hand-authoring a thirteen-family map across .agents/skills. That map is prose, nothing compares it to the 75 commands it claims to partition, and a new command joins no family without any check noticing. pm-yy8rmx already measures the inverse direction - 14 of 76 canonical commands have no declared home in the target grammar - which is the same conformance clause failing from the other side."
  "2026-08-18T19:18:16.663Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-18: active in one coupled SDK-first command-contract tranche spanning canonical flag concepts and budgets, truthful invocation arity, complete closed-domain recovery, refusal-closure scoring, source-derived executable recovery obligations, and shared CLI/MCP/completion/docs discovery metadata. This item is claimed because its acceptance surface will be edited and verified in this branch; unrelated parents and backlog items remain open and unclaimed."
  "2026-08-18T21:13:38.298Z","harness:codex","Tranche evidence: every built-in command now receives one validated capability family beside its tier; SDK resolution/listing, MCP capability projections, JSON help, and generated agent docs expose the shared tier/family contract with bidirectional coverage tests. Remaining acceptance: route human CLI help, skills/guide topics, completions, and package-contributed family declarations exclusively through the same record, add the one-screen budget, and prove one-field four-surface regeneration. Returning open and releasing ownership."
  "2026-08-23T06:39:14.688Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-23: active in a broad SDK-first contract-derived surface tranche. Live duplicate search covered all 2,538 items across open, closed, and canceled states; this canonical task retains the remaining human-help, guide/skill routing, extension-declaration, one-screen-budget, and one-field multi-surface snapshot acceptance."
  "2026-08-23T07:03:25.954Z","harness:codex","Progress: core human help now measures 41 lines/3103 UTF-8 bytes within the public one-screen budget; package command tier/family fields project through help JSON and workspace contracts; guide capabilities and generated routing derive from PM_COMMAND_CAPABILITY_CONTRACTS."
  "2026-08-23T07:10:41.427Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance (fresh /tmp/tmp.E0NPSYwToe): initialized an empty tracker, installed local pm-guide-shell and pm-command-kit packages, rendered 42-line root help with guide visible and completion hidden, observed guide core/context and command-kit standard/extensions through JSON help, resolved guide capabilities, and executed command-kit echo with two deterministic HELLO lines."
  "2026-08-23T07:20:17.847Z","harness:codex","Compatibility evidence: preserved existing public function call signatures by adding separate explicit-registry projection helpers. The SDK surface snapshot records only optional command metadata plus additive helpers/census APIs, with an explicit compatibility acknowledgement; the former root-help tests now assert core projection plus direct access to wider commands."
  "2026-08-23T08:42:00.383Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: exact full-source coverage passed at 100/100/100/100 across 566 files and 7,845 tests; pnpm lint passed including zero ESLint warnings, zero jscpd clones, 100% source/export/member docstrings, contract-derived live grammar 167/167, 117/117 executable refusal probes, tracker-context, graph-composition, and record-integrity; package artifact, secret scan, docs/skills, generated surfaces, and TypeScript package/example checks passed."
  "2026-08-23T08:50:10.418Z","harness:codex","Reviewed delivery: PR #1096 https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1096 carries the closed command-tier/capability-family implementation, generated changelog entry, exact coverage, and manual package acceptance evidence."
  "2026-08-23T08:59:58.489Z","harness:codex","Hosted smoke remediation: CI correctly detected the intentional compact root-help projection as stale token-surface baseline data. Refreshed only the measured surface baseline: root help falls from 14,060 to 3,692 bytes and the advertised per-command surface from 357,934 to 247,705 bytes; complete command discovery remains enforced separately by contract-seeded grammar 167/167."
  "2026-08-23T10:17:04.918Z","harness:codex","Review remediation evidence: CodeRabbit findings 3838168892, 3838168893, 3838168896, 3838168897, 3838168898, and 3838168904 are addressed. CHANGELOG.md is linked as reviewed documentation; command-kit anatomy now uses the executable index.ts entry; built-in help metadata is isolated from package descendants; runtime capability-family values have one canonical tuple with compile-time SDK parity; ctx is excluded from generated routing; and dynamic core help is projected against the exact rendered one-screen budget. Focused tests passed 193/193 plus cli-main-errors 129/129. Full coverage passed 7,845 tests across 566 files at statements 57,368/57,368, branches 42,912/42,912, functions 11,948/11,948, and lines 55,299/55,299. pnpm lint passed with zero ESLint warnings and zero jscpd clones; pnpm quality:static passed all gates."
